The programs in hwtests/build/ are built from the sources in hwtests/ and link two
libraries that are not part of this repository.

PSn00bSDK, by Lameguy64 and contributors. Its core libraries are under the Mozilla
Public License 2.0 and are used unmodified. Source:
https://github.com/Lameguy64/PSn00bSDK
Its licence text is in PSn00bSDK-LICENSE.md.

The common library and makefiles of ps1-tests, by Jakub Czekański. Source:
https://github.com/JaCzekanski/ps1-tests
Two tests come from its programs: mdec-step24 (with its symbols.h data, unchanged) and
cpu-code-in-irq. Their headers say which. Its licence follows.

Some tests here ask the same questions as the hardware tests in PCSX-Redux's nugget
suite (MIT, PCSX-Redux authors, https://github.com/pcsx-redux/nugget), named in their
headers. They were written afresh and contain none of its code.

